[interviewer · CLARIFY · 1:33] On the data you asked for — I'll come to that shortly. Before I give you data, is that structure MECE — what's missing or overlapping?

[candidate · 3:03] Fair challenge. I think there's overlap between my second and third buckets — commodity coffee prices and wage inflation aren't really a separate category, they're drivers of the COGS and labor lines I already listed. So I'd fold external factors in as causes rather than a parallel bucket.

On what's missing: I didn't account for anything below the operating line. Net margin, not operating margin, so interest expense matters — if they financed expansion with debt, that hits net profit without touching COGS or labor. Same for D&A on new stores and taxes.

So cleaner version: revenue, broken into price and volume and store count; operating costs, broken into COGS, labor, occupancy, and corporate; and below-the-line items — depreciation, interest, tax. External forces sit underneath as drivers.

Could I also get menu price history over the two years? That'd settle the price-versus-volume question fast.
